From eec1db4c92c43643842e4653062ba89034e182e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nipuna.dulara" <pererannd.21@uom.lk>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 13:05:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] nr: Refine the gNB and UE power models against the 3GPP
 reference

Tighten several details against TR 38.864/TR 38.840: gNB sp is now
computed against the configured reference Tx power rather than the
instantaneous one, the slot symbol count is taken from NrPhy instead of
assumed, the BS Category 2 rows are added for reference sets 2 and 3,
and RefConfigSet is made a coherent reference configuration with the
DL/UL guard period separated from the sleep transitions it used to be
folded into. Document PowerUnit as a calibration assumption rather than
a 3GPP value. On the UE side, MIMO rank is no longer treated as a
receive-chain count, UE power is charged slot-averaged for the whole
slot, and the transient/BWP-scaling API is tightened, including a fix
for the transition transient losing energy at its boundary and on
re-trigger.
